{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/902666-power-for-a-price","id":902666,"title":"Power for a price","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T06:27:10-07:00","id":902666,"title":"Power for a price","content":"So here's the deal. I love the covenants, and I think they do an awesome job of adding diversity and both conflict and opportunity. What I'm aiming to do is make their powers have a price. A price that adds to the feel of the covenant, and which somehow helps the players immerse themselves in their covenants beliefs. And I want those prices to add gameplay while also having a mechanic.<br /> <br /> For example I'm considering having The Circle of the Crone having to do a ritual sacrifice once every X days to maintain their connection to Cruac (whether Cruac comes from somthing other than themselves or if it's a matter of Dumbo &quot;needing&quot; the feather to fly is another matter). What that sacrifice is will differ according to whatever pagan beliefs the covenant has.<br /> <br /> But I'm having trouble with some of the covenants; especially the Lancea et Sanctum, because I don't want it to be about devotion to God. I don't want them to have more &quot;proof&quot; of God, although it would fuel their zealotry.<br /> <br /> So I'm hoping that you guys and girls will help me with some much needed inspiration. If you were to do something like this: what would you do?<br /> Just to be clear: my question is in regard to all the covenants, not just the Lancea et Sanctum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:39:42-07:00","id":902670,"title":"","content":"Think less actual, literal sacrifices and more &quot;Sacrifices you make for the cause&quot;. The Circle is a menagerie of cults. How does a new member feels about cutting up humans and dripping them bloodless like chickens for a religious revel? Not very human, anymore.<br /> <br /> How does a born again christian vampire feels about terrorizing the innocent, because they have to be given the opportunity to display their innocence? Again, not something a normal human entertains in his thoughts.<br /> <br /> The same can be said with human test subjects for the Dragon's Scales.<br /> <br /> Or about silencing the media to prevent a masquerade breach, as the Invictus are called to do.<br /> <br /> How does a Carthian goes about supporting another one with a radically different set of values than their own? Say, fascism?<br /> <br /> Humanity is what's at stakes. Make your players plunge into that downward spiral. Let them rail against their damnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:48:23-07:00","id":902677,"title":"","content":"I generally agree that all the Covenants involve a level of sacrifice, often measured in Humanity, but Theban Rituals already involve sacrificing items, some of them rare or valuable. You could add more of such sacrifices, certainly, if this theme needs to be expressed mystically, or play up the social aspects..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:17:26-07:00","id":902699,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The covenants do indeed involve sacrifice, and humanity is most definately a gage by which all vampires are measured. And humanity will be a big part of the campaign. But for this particular campaign I want to make the sacrifices more tangible. The price of their signature powers more demanding. And I want them to have a feel of necessity that isn't born from social expectations, but something made necessary by their own personal beliefs. <br /> <br /> Again, these may indeed be powers called forth from their blood by skill that they are merely unaware of. Or they may indeed come from somewhere else, whether that be nature, spirits or whatever else. I want there to be doubt, but something that makes the players feel as if there is something more.<br /> Dumbo is currently my best example. He was able to fly without the feather, but he believed in the power of the feather with such intensity that his own psyche made it a necessity. Whether or not there actually are gods, spirits or realms from which vitae can draw power or if the power is their own is somewhat irrelevant at this stage of the planning. <br /> <br /> My intent is that the price of the power is something in their behavior or something happening as a consequence of the frame of thought their philosphy demands - and not only the ingredients for the rituals in Theban sorcery or the blood sacrifice Cruac. And I want each covenant to have something similar. Something to play on the concept of &quot;faith/philosphy/ideoligy&quot; or &quot;power&quot; other than someone tellling you what you are supposed to do.<br /> I know that this isn't the way the system intends things to be, but it's something that'll benefit my players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T07:46:17-07:00","id":902716,"title":"","content":"Well, both ritual magics already give you bonuses to casting if you provide sacrifices above and beyond the usual. Play that angle up, or make them a requirement for some rituals, and that answers that.<br /> <br /> For Oaths, you could require the sipping of vitae of the other, creating a bond and fueling addiction in the Invictus. Carthian Law is difficult, because that is all about the power of Consensus. Its the unconcious Beasts of their covenant joining forces and working their magic through rules and regulations. This requires politics and socializing and smoozing for favor and popularity. Not really sure how to make that anything cost things beyond the time and energy invested.<br /> <br /> Coils and Scales? You've got to run some insane cray-cray experiments on yourself and others. I think injecting yourself with bleach is its own payment for power. Just focus on the inhumane experiments before letting someone buy or use an Ordo power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:20:37-07:00","id":902732,"title":"","content":"My ideas might be more social constructs than what you are looking for, but some thoughts:<br /> <br /> What if for the Lance it was less about their own devotion, and more that of interactions with others. Works, rather than faith. It still has a religious connotation, but forces interactions. These interactions might be different depending on the Sanctified archetype of the character. Shepherds would tend to the flock, punishing wicked mortals and tempting the saintly. Crusaders would need to strike fear into the Church's enemies. Priests would seek out confessions. So, a Theban Sorcerer who doesn't upkeep an active connection with others (works) loses their connection with the discipline.<br /> <br /> For Invictus, I think Blood Oaths make a natural effect-point. Maybe Invictus members are expected to have two oaths at all times. One Oath that pledges them to a superior, and a second Oath they hold over a minion, servant or inferior of some sort. I personally enjoy that power dynamic in the Invictus: Being a good servant, rival and leader all at the same time. Invictus which eschew the ladder/pyramid and go Oathless aren't as trusted and begin to lose access to the advantages. So you're struggling at both ends, as it were. Trying to be a good tool for your boss, but also trying to be a good boss for your own workers - cause if either ditches out on you, it affects your place in the Covenant.<br /> <br /> For Ordo, what's the College Professor mantra? Publish or Perish? The Defiant could need to be actively working on a project - either funding, running or observing - to keep their own chrysalises from dissipating. This one doesn't ring as true for me, though, as the changes from the Mysteries are supposed to be permanent. Though I do remember alternate rules for the chrysalis somewhere - the Ordo book I think, that pre-loaded the process. So there was an element of sacrifice or risk every time a new coil is learned. Rather than upkeep, then, you can make it a difficult change in and of itself that doesn't always work. I think there was an XP cost for failure in those alt rules, though, which I would ditch - just make the sacrifice conflict and time and the threat of having to redo an entire experiment/process - and really make the PCs come up with interesting experiements for learning each dot, or at the minimum finding a mentor that already has a pre-loaded experiment (that you) made.<br /> <br /> Carthians I think should be in tune with the Law somehow. You could also go public services, but I think that could get into the goody-two-shoes conception of the Carthians that I personally dislike. Carthian Law seems to have really made a push more toward an objective force, the same kind of force that gives the Traditions their mechanics. Quite simply, then, Carthians who break the Law suffer a consequence. I'd probably define the Law from the frame of the Covenant, though, not <i>necessarily </i>the domain laws, as that could cause some fun conflict when the Domain and Covenant are at cross purposes over an issue and the PC is in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:28:17-07:00","id":902735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyMann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/902666-power-for-a-price?p=902699#post902699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that this isn't the way the system intends things to be, but it's something that'll benefit my players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>How so, exactly ?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I guess for the Invictus, you could be asked to give away money or a certain number of mortals to the Invictus' local leaders. None of the lower members of the Invictus knows where that stuff goes. Maybe this fuels a slavery ring and other criminal investigations out of town, suggesting a global conspiracy, maybe a powerful elder needs humans to feed himself or his childers that then feed him. Not to mention that if you use the ivictus oaths, they can be forced to be constantly under an oath.<br /> <br /> Not sure about the Carthians. I'm already not a fan of Carthians and Invictus having a form of sorcery (especially carthians), and aside from an immediate loyalty to the cause, I don't really see. Although there was an idea of a global conspiracy of carthians in &quot;The Danse Macabre&quot; supplement. They were setting up test towns in remote places where they tried to have humans and vampires live together without masquerade. So in the same way, you could be asked to provide humans or money for one of these places, whether you know it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T12:37:13-07:00","id":902941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/902666-power-for-a-price?p=902735#post902735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so, exactly ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on which part you're asking about. But I'll answer both things to the best of my ability <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <u><b>- How the system doesn't intend what I'm trying to do:</b></u><br /> To me the authors have made some interesting covenants which have their own unique world views and their own unique mechanical strengths. But they have no mechancal weaknesses, nothing mechanical that ties them to their power - other than social status. But status is already a big part of the game, and something to be desired no matter where you are. And I want the covenants to have a downside, like the clans have banes that'll come into play sooner or later.<br /> I don't see the system balancing the good with the bad <i><u>in the way I desire for this particular campaign</u></i>. I want something dark to be at the core of their power to add to the reasons why each covenant wants to keep their praxis a secret. <br /> You want cruac? Well, the pagan lord you worship demands that you sacrifice the blood of the living every month, or maybe it wants secrets to be ripped from your brain, or the enslavement of others. Does it work? who knows! But when you perform the sacrifice you can practice Cruac until the next sacrifice. <br /> You want to bind other kindred with the oaths of the Invictus? Well to do that you must feed regularly on the blood of other kindred or your oaths will be no more than mere words. Or maybe they are bound to the life of one of your ghouls for some reason. Why is this? There are many theories, but no one has ever maintained an oath unless they've done what needed to be done.<br /> You want to trancend vampirism? Guess what, your humanity is in the way and has to be stripped from your soul by some dark torture that you've concocted. Can you regain that humanity? sure, if you work at it. But growing closer to the beast is what makes the effect permanent.<br /> <br /> These are just quick examples and not necessarily something I'll choose, but I like the fact that it gives the covenant a dark secret in regard to their power. Something that if it got out would set the covenants members at a disadvantage because it could be used against them. You made a deal with the invictus that you want out of? make sure his batch of vitae never makes it to his door. The circles cruac has you scared to confront an enemy, disrupt his sacrifice somehow. Etc. etc.<br /> <br /> The system invites us to keep the secrets of the covenants so we won't lose standing. And that's dangerous. But I want to dig deeper than that, and make the &quot;truth&quot; of the covenants something darker. And it makes the power kind of like a drug; you need to fix in order to get your high.<br /> <br /> I'm having a hard time translating my thoughts into english, so I apoligize it my ramble doesn't make sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <u><b>- How it's good for my players:</b></u><br /> They have a tendency to choose a clan or class or whatever based on the power it affords them, with little thought for what's expected of them. And we've had fun with this. But they've grown accustomed to this and they need something other than NPC approval to make them <i><b>want</b></i> to do what needs to be done. And they're asking for it. Other than that, this will give them something to focus on when they at some point don't know what else to do. It adds to the drama, and the players like being challenged with &quot;do this or shit happens&quot; scenarios, and this lets them choose some of the &quot;shit happens&quot; I throw at them. <br /> You want power? Sure go right ahead. But you have to work for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> another reason why a character may fit into one covenant and not another.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b... I hope all this makes at least some kind of sense to you guys :P haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:44:48-07:00","id":903612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyMan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>- How it's good for my players:</b></u><br /> They have a tendency to choose a clan or class or whatever based on the power it affords them, with little thought for what's expected of them. And we've had fun with this. But they've grown accustomed to this and they need something other than NPC approval to make them <i><b>want</b></i> to do what needs to be done. And they're asking for it. Other than that, this will give them something to focus on when they at some point don't know what else to do. It adds to the drama, and the players like being challenged with &quot;do this or shit happens&quot; scenarios, and this lets them choose some of the &quot;shit happens&quot; I throw at them.<br /> You want power? Sure go right ahead. But you have to work for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> another reason why a character may fit into one covenant and not another.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b... I hope all this makes at least some kind of sense to you guys :P haha</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think what you're suggesting will acomplish your goal. Its simply an extra hoop to jump through for powers, but once done, its no matter. I mean, okay, live sacrifice once a month. The CotC love group rituals. Who's going to want to interrupt that?<br /> <br /> I think you would be better off making the covenant Mentors have demands and favors to be paid before teaching things. You learn nothing without paying a price to a Mentor of somekind, leaving yourself in debt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-30-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}